From 09e40328d28fd6e2731d246e70ec89ff1fa7ae37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emscripten-forge <recipes@emscripten-forge>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 23:39:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Drop foreigncall table entries that no longer exist

src/interpreter-foreigncall.c is generated (generate_interpreter_foreigncall.jl
in Keno/julia-wasm) from the headers of the day. Remove the entries whose
targets are gone, so that the runtime links without undefined symbols:

- emscripten's coroutine API, emscripten_yield, emscripten_sleep_with_yield,
  the IndexedDB blob functions and emscripten_worker_respond* were removed
  from emscripten
- dSFMT's old-style names (init_gen_rand, genrand_close_open, ...) are only
  declared when DSFMT_DO_NOT_USE_OLD_NAMES is not defined, which is how
  julia (and the emscripten-forge dsfmt package) builds it
- jl_apply_2va, jl_gc_use, jl_threading_profile, jl_dump_fptr_asm and
  jl_deserialize_verify_header do not exist in this runtime

Also fix the declaration of emscripten_wget, which returns int; the
mismatch made wasm-ld replace the call with a trap.
